---
title: Redaction Checker
description: Test a redacted PDF for leaks. Find text under black bars, hidden text, redactions that were not applied, earlier versions and metadata. Runs in your browser. Nothing is uploaded.
---

<section class="tool-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <%= partial "partials/brand" %>
    <h1>Redaction Checker</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Test a redacted PDF before you share it. Find text that is covered on the page but still in the file.
      Your PDF is never uploaded.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tool">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="drop" id="drop">
      <p class="drop-title">Drop a redacted PDF here</p>
      <p class="drop-text">or choose a file.</p>
      <div class="drop-actions">
        <label class="button">
          Choose a PDF
          <input type="file" id="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" class="visually-hidden">
        </label>
        <button type="button" id="sample" class="button button-outline">Try a badly redacted example</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="status" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

    <div class="editor" id="editor" hidden>
      <div class="editor-foot">
        <div class="editor-actions">
          <button type="button" id="new" class="button button-outline">Check another PDF</button>
          <button type="button" id="download" class="button">Download report</button>
        </div>
        <p class="download-note" id="download-note" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>

      <div class="findings" id="findings"></div>

      <div class="pdf-pages" id="pages"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="notes">
      <div>
        <h3>What it checks</h3>
        <p>Text under black bars or white boxes, white or invisible text, redactions that were marked but not applied, earlier versions saved in the file, comments, form values, attached files and metadata.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>How to fix a leak</h3>
        <p>Use the <a href="/tools/pdf-redactor/">PDF Redactor</a>. It makes a new PDF from images of the pages, so no text, earlier versions or metadata stay in the file.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Private by design</h3>
        <p>The page has no server code and uses no AI model. <a href="https://mozilla.github.io/pdf.js/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PDF.js</a> reads the PDF and draws the pages in your browser.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="module" src="/javascripts/tools/redaction-checker.js"></script>
